<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Heavy consortium wins $500 mln Vietnam order.</title>
<headline>Korea Heavy consortium wins $500 mln Vietnam order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Heavy Industries and Construction Co Ltd said on Wednesday it has won an order for a $500 million coal-fired thermal power plant in Vietnam in partnership with Japan's Nissho Iwai Corp and Anglo-French power firm GEC Alsthom.  </p>
<p>Korea Heavy said in a statement the 600-megawatt plant order was given by Electricity of Vietnam.</p>
<p>The consortium is due to complete the construction in PhaLai, HaiHung, 50 km east of Hanoi, 40 months after the contract is signed, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;The formal agreement will be signed soon,&quot; said a company spokesman.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
